::ingredients

(cheese, mid-aged, not too savoury or delicate) 2 slices
(sugar) to taste
(cinnamon) to taste
(frying fat) = (butter) as needed -OR- (lard) as needed

::equipment

(pan)

::instructions

(frying fat) <heat, pan, for frying>
    + (cheese) <place>
    + (sugar) + (cinnamon) <sprinkle, immediately, all over>
(cheese) <remove, as soon as softened>
    <serve, warm>

::story

Casio in pastelletto means roughly "cheese treat" in vernacular Italian.

It is a medieval recipe and the taste changes a lot depending on the cheese you choose, so there are no exact quantities for the ingredients, and the dish may be considered a main one or a sweet (I think it was probably a dessert, though).
You will probably have to do some trial and error before you get a good result.

